      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 40334,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "TRAP 1  Go has NO generational GC - allocating millions of short-lived objects still costs GC work (no Eden fast-lane)\nTRAP 2  GOGC=100 means GC fires when live heap doubles -> high allocation rate = frequent GC -> tune GOGC for your workload\nTRAP 3  Goroutine stack growth copies ALL frames -> avoid deeply recursive functions with large local arrays on stack",
      "fontSize": 13,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "TRAP 1  Go has NO generational GC - allocating millions of short-lived objects still costs GC work (no Eden fast-lane)\nTRAP 2  GOGC=100 means GC fires when live heap doubles -> high allocation rate = frequent GC -> tune GOGC for your workload\nTRAP 3  Goroutine stack growth copies ALL frames -> avoid deeply recursive functions with large local arrays on stack",
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
